<p>The <code>{pad:ignore}{pad:calendar}{/pad:ignore}</code> tag draws a month with its events - from a <code>{pad:ignore}{pad:data}{/pad:ignore}</code>
block, a page array or a <code>_data</code> file. The arrows move a month; today is marked.</p>

{pad:calendar data='agenda', title='what'/}

<p><code>{pad:ignore}{pad:calendar data='agenda', title='what'}{/pad:ignore}</code></p>

<h2>Your own markup</h2>

<p>As a pair the tag hands over the weeks and their days as rows - <code>$day</code>, <code>$date</code>,
<code>$today</code>, <code>$count</code>, <code>$class</code>, the day's <code>events</code> - so a
mini calendar with a dot per busy day is a few lines:</p>

<table class="mini">
  <tr><th>Mo</th><th>Tu</th><th>We</th><th>Th</th><th>Fr</th><th>Sa</th><th>Su</th></tr>
  {pad:calendar data='agenda'}
  <tr>
    {array:days}<td class="{$class}" title="{$date}">{$day}{pad:if $count gt 0}<i></i>{/pad:if}</td>{/array:days}
  </tr>
  {/pad:calendar}
</table>

<pre>{pad:ignore}{pad:calendar data='agenda'}
  &lt;tr&gt;
    {array:days}&lt;td class="{$class}"&gt;{$day}{pad:if $count gt 0}&lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;{/pad:if}&lt;/td&gt;{/array:days}
  &lt;/tr&gt;
{/pad:calendar}{/pad:ignore}</pre>
